.\" lsusb.1 - list USB devices
.Dd March 14, 2026
.Dt LSUSB 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm lsusb
.Nd list USB devices
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl t
.Op Fl s Ar bus Ns : Ns Ar devnum
.Op Fl d Ar vendor Ns : Ns Ar product
.Op Fl V
.Op Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility enumerates USB devices attached to the system and displays
summary information for each device.
By default, a one-line summary is printed for every device showing the
bus number, device address, vendor ID, and product ID.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v
Verbose mode.
Display detailed USB descriptor information for each device, including
device, configuration, interface, and endpoint descriptors.
String descriptors are retrieved where available.
.It Fl t
Tree mode.
Display USB devices in a tree topology showing bus and port hierarchy.
.It Fl s Ar bus Ns : Ns Ar devnum
Show only the device with the specified bus number and/or device
number.
Either field may be omitted to match all values for that field.
Values are in decimal.
.It Fl d Ar vendor Ns : Ns Ar product
Show only devices with the specified vendor and/or product ID.
Either field may be omitted to match all values for that field.
Values are in hexadecimal.
.It Fl V
Print version information and exit.
.It Fl h
Print usage information and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
List all USB devices:
.Pp
.Dl $ lsusb
.Pp
List all devices on bus 1:
.Pp
.Dl $ lsusb -s 1:
.Pp
Show verbose information for a specific vendor:product:
.Pp
.Dl $ lsusb -v -d 1d6b:0002
.Pp
Show device tree:
.Pp
.Dl $ lsusb -t
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libusb 3 ,
.Xr usb 4
.Sh AUTHORS
Substrate contributors.
